      "routePreference": "preferred",
      "explanationAfterStep": "The phenyl group moves from carbon to oxygen with its bonding pair as the O–O bond breaks. The group that migrates is the one best able to carry a partial positive charge in the transition state: tertiary alkyl > secondary alkyl ≈ phenyl > primary alkyl > methyl. So an oxygen atom is inserted between the carbonyl carbon and the ring, not the methyl."
    },
